module gunbc.plans.ci_process_end_to_end

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn ci_process_end_to_end_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Goal:** make CI consume shared execution, Materialization, Placement and secrets/effects authorities, priced in displaced CI delay. This ROADMAP §1 charter is the whole push→execution chain; linked carriers own individual slices. The [2026-06-22 audit and #5427 run 27924855136](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/ci_process_end_to_end.dag) are historical observations, not current deployment or timing claims."),
    p(text: "**Historical boundary (2026-06-22 audit):** ci_workflow.dag → ci_yaml_emit → committed ci.yml was derived and drift-gated by ci_yaml_gate; GitHub dispatch, concurrency evaluation, placement and final check remain external. A generated invocation can still be stale at bootstrap because GitHub reads the committed file. The historical floor invoked claim_executor with gunbc_ci_floor_plan, derived dependency batches, read live cgroup budgets, selected memory_aware_spawn_width and affected witnesses, then returned its verdict to GitHub/dashboard. Derived description and executing workload do not prove modeled host operation: placement, runner registration/count/labels and caps were hand-managed, joined only by labels and one-way budget reads."),
    p(text: "**Method:** (1) derive runner count and caps from operator_fleet + ResourceEnvelope, generate and drift-gate deployment, proving aggregate peaks fit host capacity; (2) enable the proven-pure resolve cache where still applicable; (3) subject to the operator decision, emit cross-host placement from fleet authority; (4) extend affected selection into Rust work; (5) collapse duplicate PR/workflow_dispatch runs; (6) classify cross-run clustered exit-137 as Infra, with both kill handlers represented as one fact and a fail-closed clustering discriminator, before merge-freshness LIVE. Keep operator_fleet whether placement is built or deferred. Current DESIGN migration/model rules govern these historical steps."),
    p(text: "**Measured bottleneck hypothesis:** the old atomic Rust gate combined compile and run time without measuring their split; time cargo test --no-run before selecting a fix. Safe Cargo concurrency must derive from cores, pids and memory rather than the sccache crash clamp. Expose Rust test partitions to the same placement authority, avoid cold repeated resolution, and remove affected-set-independent run-all work. Parallelism inside the Rust node is distinct from arbitrary sharding/tiering knobs: no second scheduler or hand-set utilization budget. Historical serial ingest/self-host subshells also require inspection. Re-measure the current pipeline before treating old mechanisms as live."),
    p(text: "**Validate:** whole-tree compile-clean plus a deliberately failing compile control; executing corpus/gates and self-host closure; workflow drift/freshness/exists guards; deployment/cap drift refusals; resource-derived scheduling under contention; cache semantic equivalence; affected Rust coverage; duplicate dispatch and merge-freshness witnesses. The stage0 seed --verify gate was an open emission gap in the audit, not established completion. Concurrency uses witness_floor_concurrency_group/policy; bare dispatch alone falls back to run_id. The per-main unique-run coverage drop is gunbc.rung_drop.main_per_commit_floor_verdict."),
    p(text: "**Shared owners:** converge sccache, resolve, RecordedFixture and BuildBuddy through realize(subject); ParseTable memo was deleted by R2 on 2026-10-08. Jobs, threads and sessions consume one Placement authority; BMC/tokens/cache authentication consume one secrets/effects model. Decision completeness belongs to std.decision, not the removed RealizationObjective.goals. Each abstraction must gain a non-test CI consumer; taxonomy alone is not progress. Eventual gunbhub ownership of the external engine is not the immediate timeliness requirement."),
    p(text: "**Open decisions:** operator sets the target CI ceiling; either build placement now or delete/fence its inert predicate under one named runway; confirm CI as the ROADMAP integration workload. Steps 1, 2, 4 and 5 do not depend on that choice. The retirement condition below remains the completion contract; follow gunbc.plans.ci_merge_freshness and docs/plans/ci-end-to-end-accounting.md for the related authorities."),
  ]
}

data ci_process_end_to_end_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "ci-process-end-to-end",
  title: "CI, end to end — what's on `.dag` today, what isn't, and the lane that closes the gap",
  body: ci_process_end_to_end_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this doc when §3-B (the fabric operation — placement, runner deployment, per-runner caps) is on `.dag` and drift-gated (steps 1 + 3 landed), the resolve cache is enabled in CI (step 2), and the rust tentpole no longer dominates a CI run — at which point the push→execute chain is on fabric except GitHub's irreducible engine, the §4 scheduling/caching gaps are closed by a real non-test consumer, and this charter's gap-map is a witnessed property rather than an audit.")
  }
}
